## Hold to be placed

A notice under Section 168 read with Section 94 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita has been received through CFCFRMS for the complaint(s) above [BNSS-168] [BNSS-94]. As per the SOP, please put on hold the amount equivalent to the disputed amount received in A/c No. {{ s.account_id }} vide UTR/TRX ID {{ s.utrs }} on {{ s.inflow_dates }} [SOP-9-1] [SOP-ANNEX-I].

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Disputed amount received | {{ s.disputed_amount }} |
| Balance at assessment | {{ s.balance_now }} |
| Victim money still in the account | {{ s.tainted_amount }} |
| **Hold amount** | **{{ s.hold_amount }}** |
{% if c.has_forward_hold %}
| Forward hold on future credits | {{ s.forward_hold_amount }} |
{% endif %}

{% if c.mode == "pool" %}
The merchant's order for this payment is not delivered. Cancel the order and keep {{ s.hold_amount }} on hold in the pool / nodal account for this payment instead of restricting the merchant's account [SOP-9-2].
{% elif c.mode == "intermediary" %}
A/c No. {{ s.account_id }} is a {{ c.intermediary_label }} account operated for a payment aggregator or other intermediary, and CFCFRMS has notified action against it. Hold only the disputed amount of {{ s.hold_amount }} in this nodal / pool / escrow account [SOP-9-1-III]. Do not suspend digital banking or seize the account; operations for other customers' funds continue [SOP-9-1-III]. No forward hold is marked on nodal, pool or escrow accounts [SOP-9-1-I].
{% elif c.mode == "forward_only" %}
No victim money is available in the account now, so no amount is to be held today (hold amount {{ s.hold_amount }}). Mark only the forward hold described below.
{% else %}
Place the hold for {{ s.hold_amount }} only: the victim money still in the account, capped at the available balance.
{% endif %}
{% if c.account_level %}
The hold of {{ s.hold_amount }} is the amount recoverable for the victims [SOP-9-1] [SOP-ANNEX-I]. In addition, an exceptional account-level hold applies to this account: the officer requested it on recorded reasons and a supervisor approved it (see the approved request). Amount-specific holds remain the default [SOP-5-IX].
{% else %}
This is an amount-specific hold, not a freeze of the account; other funds and digital banking remain available [SOP-5-IX] [SOP-9-1] [SOP-ANNEX-I]. High Courts have indicated that a lien on the identifiable disputed amount, rather than a whole-account freeze, is the proper course [CASE-NEELKANTH] [CASE-SHREE-BALAJI]. Account-level action is taken only as a recorded, supervisor-approved exception.
{% endif %}
{% if c.has_forward_hold %}

## Forward hold (first-layer account)

A/c No. {{ s.account_id }} is a first-layer account and its balance is below the disputed amount [SOP-DEF-FIRST-LAYER]. Forward holds are placed only on first-layer accounts, never on nodal, pool or escrow accounts [SOP-9-1-I]. Mark a forward hold on future credits up to {{ s.forward_hold_amount }}: the victim money this account has already sent to cash-out points or to untraced destinations. A forward hold is not money in hand and is not counted as recoverable.
{% endif %}
{% if c.is_innocent %}

## Innocent-holder handling

{% if c.is_conduit %}
The account appears to have been used as a pass-through by someone else, without the knowledge, connivance or consent of the account holder (unwitting conduit) [SOP-5-XII]. Hold the amount only: no escalation. There is no automatic STR: because the account was used as a conduit, an STR is recommended and the officer decides whether to file it [PMLR-2-1-G]. An enhanced due diligence memo accompanies this instruction, and the holder may file a grievance for review of the hold [SOP-10-1].
{% else %}
The account holder appears to have received the money in good faith, without knowledge of, connivance in or consent to the fraud (bona fide recipient) [SOP-5-XII]. Hold the amount only: no escalation and no STR by default; the officer decides if new facts emerge. An enhanced due diligence memo accompanies this instruction, and the holder may file a grievance for review of the hold [SOP-10-1].
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if c.escalate %}

## Escalation flag: human decision required

This account is flagged ESCALATE_S106_CANDIDATE because {{ c.escalation_basis }}. The flag is advisory and does not change the hold above, which stays amount-specific. Seizure under Section 106 BNSS needs a registered FIR, and a debit freeze of the account needs an order of the Magistrate under Section 107 BNSS [BNSS-106] [BNSS-107]. Banks may only place the disputed amount under lien [CASE-KARTIK-CHATUR]. The nodal officer must decide before any further step is taken.
